cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TreeRing, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "TreeRing: least-knowledge security layer for LLM agents"
abstract: >-
  TreeRing is an open-source security layer for LLM agents that defends against
  prompt injection by isolation rather than detection. A privileged planner never
  sees untrusted data, quarantined readers have no tools, values between modules
  are restricted to declared schemas and carry provenance tags, and every decision
  is appended to a tamper-evident hash-chained audit log with human-in-the-loop
  approval where policy requires it. The design is inspired by tree rings
  (dendrochronology), which record each year's conditions as a by-product of growth.
authors:
